    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Enjoying a prime position overlooking a family-friendly amenity green within the much sought-after Archers Wood development, this spacious four-bedroom modern home combines generous living accommodation with a sunny south-west facing back garden and parking for three cars.\r\nBuilt by Cairn Homes, Number 17 is one of the development’s larger four-bedroom house types, extending to approximately 145 sq. m / 1,565 sq. ft. Bright, spacious and well-proportioned throughout, the property has been thoughtfully designed with modern family living in mind. \r\nAt the heart of the home is a contemporary kitchen/dining room, finished to a high standard with quartz worktops and integrated appliances, and opening directly onto the back garden. Extra-height ground floor ceilings and large windows enhance the overall feeling of light and space, while a separate living room provides a comfortable second reception space.\r\nUpstairs are four well-proportioned bedrooms, with fitted wardrobes to the double bedrooms, together with the main family bathroom and ensuite. High-quality sanitary ware, contemporary tiling and heated towel rails are among the features included in the original Archers Wood specification.\r\nThe property is also highly energy efficient, with an A2 BER rating, air-to-water heat pump, dual-zone heating controls, high levels of insulation and high-performance double glazing. Modern conveniences include Cat 6 broadband wiring, USB charging points and a generous provision of electrical sockets, while the house was also future proofed for an EV charging point and garden office connection.\r\nOutside, Number 17 enjoys an excellent position within the development. To the front, it directly overlooks a landscaped green, creating an attractive open outlook and a wonderful amenity for families, while the driveway provides off-street parking for three cars.\r\nTo the rear, the south-west facing back garden is ideally positioned to enjoy afternoon and evening sunshine, making it a great space for outdoor dining, entertaining friends or simply relaxing in the sun.\r\nArchers Wood itself has been thoughtfully planned around its natural setting, with more than 20 acres of landscaped open space incorporating greens, playgrounds, sports facilities, wildflower meadows and woodland walks. The Three Trouts Way provides an attractive stream-side walking route through mature woodland. \r\nThe development is conveniently located close to Delgany village and within easy reach of Greystones, with its excellent choice of shops, cafés, restaurants, schools, sports clubs, beaches, marina and DART station. The nearby N11 provides convenient access to Dublin and the M50. \r\nCombining a larger four-bedroom house type, excellent specification, green outlook and sunny south-west facing garden, Number 17 is an ideal choice for families seeking a spacious, energy-efficient modern home.\r\nCall us today to arrange a viewing of this must-see family home."
      },
      {
